R"VG(
# industrial7.vg (H-04's second pass): a pinned bundle of telegrams (a writer and a reader of a family, `@cast letter`) and a works' rules,
# moved here from industrial5.vg as it grew.

# ---- the telegrams -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
genre.telegram (words=24..80)
  {@cast letter}{tg.head}\n{tg.one}\n{tg.two}\n{tg.three}
  {@cast letter}{tg.head}\n{tg.one}\n{tg.two}\n{tg.three}\n{tg.four}

tg.head (formula)
  Telegrams, kept together with a pin:
  Three forms from the telegraph office, folded together:
  Telegrams, in a {colour.any} envelope:

tg.one
  To {$you:name}, {$you.home}: {tg.arrived} stop {tg.ask1} stop {$me:name}
  To {$you:name}, {$you.home}: {tg.news} stop {tg.ask1} stop {$me:name}
  To {$you:name}, {$you.home}: {tg.news} stop home by {festival} stop {$me:name}
tg.arrived
  arrived safe
  (inv.railway=1) arrived safe the train was late
  arrived safe the roads were bad
  arrived tired but whole
  here at last
tg.news
  news good
  the post is mine
  the {herd} sold well
  sold everything at a good price
  the work is harder than they said
  mother better
  the house is let
  lost the case
  married yesterday no fuss {=.wed}
  need money not much {=.money}
tg.ask1
  write
  wire back
  explain later
  tell nobody
  send {n} {coin} {=.money}
  meet the boat
  keep my room

tg.two
  To {$me:name}, {$me.home}: {tg.reply} stop {tg.ask2} stop {$you:name}
tg.reply
  glad
  (.money=1) money sent
  (.money=1) no money explain
  (.wed=1) congratulations to you both
  come home
  it is not good
  mother asks when
  the {herd} are sick
  the roof fell in
  your letter came after you
tg.ask2
  explain now
  write properly
  answer
  do nothing yet
  come for {festival}
  bring {crop}

tg.three
  To {$you:name}, {$you.home}: {tg.end} stop {tg.end2} stop {$me:name}
tg.end
  coming
  cannot come the line is closed
  coming by the {ind.tg.time} post
  will explain everything
  not coming after all
  (stage>=1) leave now do not wait for me
ind.tg.time
  first
  evening
  night
tg.end2
  love to all
  tell mother
  bring the {garment.n}
  keep the {beast} in
  (inv.railway=1) do not meet the train
  meet the boat
  say nothing to the neighbours
  the {crop} is in

tg.four
  To {$me:name}, {$me.home}: {tg.last} stop {tg.last2} stop {$you:name}
tg.last
  understood
  waiting
  the light is on
  come quickly
  never mind

tg.last2
  the {herd} are well
  {n} {coin} under the stone
  the house is cold without you
  the {festival} songs are being practised
  the {colour.any} door is open
  mind the river

# ---- the factory's rules -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
genre.rules (words=40..150)
  {rules.head} {rules.item} {rules.item} {rules.item} {rules.item} {rules.end}
  {rules.head} {rules.item} {rules.item} {rules.item} {rules.item} {rules.item} {rules.end}

rules.head (formula)
  Rules of the {$home} {ledger.what}, to be obeyed by all hands:
  The rules of the {craft} works, posted by order of the owners:
  To all who work here, the rules, which are not to be argued with:

rules.item
  (once) Work begins at the {rules.bell} bell and ends at the last. A hand late by {rules.late} loses {rules.loses}.
  (once) No talking at the {rules.machine}.
  (once) No lamps in the {rules.store}, on any account.
  (once) A hand who is sick sends word by {rules.word}; a hand who sends no word {rules.punish}.
  (once) Wages are paid at the end of the week, at the office, and not at the gate, in {coin} and not in {crop}.
  (once) The doors are locked during work. The key is with {rules.keyholder}.
  (once) Children under {n} are not to work at the {rules.machine}.
  (once) Any damage to the {rules.machine} is paid for out of wages.
  (once) The works are closed on the rest day and on {festival}, and for {feast.custom}, by custom.
  (once) No {drink} is to be brought into the yard, nor drunk in the yard, nor smelt on anyone in the yard.
  (once) No {beast} is to be brought to work, however well it behaves, nor fed from the {rules.store}.
  (once) The {fuel} is counted every night; a hand found with any {rules.punish}.
  (once) Any hand found {rules.fault} {rules.punish}.
  (once) Any hand found {rules.fault} {rules.punish}.
  (once) There is to be no {ind.sport} in the dinner hour, by order, after the broken window.
  (once) Hands will wash at the trough before the noon meal and not in the {watersrc.n}.
  (once) Singing is permitted on {festival} eve only, and then not the song about {rules.songabout}.
  (once) The {craft} goods are not to be taken home, even spoiled ones, even for a wedding.
  (once) A collection for the family of a hand killed at the {rules.machine} is made by the owners and not by the hands, and paid in {coin}.

rules.bell
  first
  morning
  {nth}
rules.late
  a quarter of an hour
  the length of a prayer
  the time it takes to boil water
rules.loses
  half a day
  the day's {drink}
  {n} {smallcoin}
rules.machine
  machines
  looms
  presses
  vats
  furnaces
  saws
rules.store
  store room
  {fuel} shed
  drying loft
  {craft} sheds
rules.word
  the morning
  a child or a neighbour
  the first bell
rules.keyholder
  the foreman
  the owner's son
  the night watchman, who is deaf
rules.fault
  asleep at the {rules.machine}
  smoking in the {rules.store}
  with a {beast} in the yard
  drunk on {drink}
  teaching the young hands the song about the foreman
  out of the yard without leave
  gambling at {rules.pastime} in the dinner hour
rules.punish
  loses a day's pay
  is fined {n} {smallcoin}
  is dismissed without a character
  will answer to the owners
  cleans the yard on the rest day
rules.pastime
  dice
  cards
  knucklebones
rules.end (formula)
  By order of the owners.
  Any hand who does not like the rules may go.
  Posted at the gate, year {#year:digits}.
  The foreman's word is final.
rules.songabout
  the foreman
  the owners' wives
  the {craft} masters
  the night watchman
)VG"
